{"name":"Grand Canal","hex":"#3c797d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Grand Canal","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A channel in Venice, Italy. It forms one of the major water-traffic corridors in the city.","A channel in China."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Grand_Canal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grand Canal (China)","blocks":[{"text":"The Grand Canal is a system of interconnected canals linking various major rivers and lakes in North and East China, serving as an important waterborne transport infrastructure between the north and the south during Medieval and premodern China. It is the longest artificial waterway in the world and a World Heritage Site."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Wanning_Bridge_1.jpg/330px-Wanning_Bridge_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Canal_(China)","wikidata":"Q31347"},{"title":"Grand Canal (Ireland)","blocks":[{"text":"The Grand Canal is the southernmost of a pair of canals that connect Dublin, in the east of Ireland, with the River Shannon in the west, via Tullamore and a number of other villages and towns, the two canals nearly encircling Dublin's inner city. Its sister canal on the Northside of Dublin is the Royal Canal. The last working cargo barge passed through the Grand Canal in 1960."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Grand_Canal_Dublin_2006.jpg/330px-Grand_Canal_Dublin_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Canal_(Ireland)","wikidata":"Q1542537"},{"title":"Canal","blocks":[{"text":"Canals or artificial waterways are waterways or engineered channels built for drainage management or for conveyancing water transport vehicles. They carry free, calm surface flow under atmospheric pressure, and can be thought of as artificial rivers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Alter_Strom.jpg/330px-Alter_Strom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canal","wikidata":"Q12284"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Grand-Canal.png/500px-Grand-Canal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Grand-Canal.png/500px-Grand-Canal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand-Canal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sui_Wendi_Tang.jpg/500px-Sui_Wendi_Tang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sui_Wendi_Tang.jpg/500px-Sui_Wendi_Tang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASui_Wendi_Tang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sui_Yangdi_Tang.jpg/500px-Sui_Yangdi_Tang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Sui_Yangdi_Tang.jpg/500px-Sui_Yangdi_Tang.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASui_Yangdi_Tang.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Pound_Lock_System.gif/330px-Pound_Lock_System.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Pound_Lock_System.gif/330px-Pound_Lock_System.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Chinese invention of the pound lock system allows for water